  "question": {
    "text": "There are two balls in an urn. Each ball can be either white or black. If a white ball is put into the urn and there after a ball is drawn at random from the urn, then the probability that it is white is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Q8laS",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wS9fN",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "haQs5",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{5}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Dxc8A",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total possible event when one ball is taken out $={ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_1$ Let $E$ : The event of 1 white ball coming out\nNo. of ways to 1 white ball coming out $={ }^2 \\mathrm{C}_1$\n$$\n\\therefore P(E)=\\frac{{ }^2 C_1}{{ }^3 C_1}=\\frac{2}{3}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
